# What `mcpb pack` must NOT put inside the .mcpb bundle.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The bundle is a SECOND public distribution surface, on
# top of the npm tarball, and the two have different default contents. npm ships
# only the `files` allowlist in package.json (src, README, LICENSE, CHANGELOG),
# but `mcpb pack` starts from the whole working directory, so everything the npm
# allowlist quietly excluded gets swept in unless it is named here.
#
# MEASURED before this file was added: a test pack produced a 3.4MB bundle
# containing .claude/RESUME.md, the full test/ directory and scripts/. Those
# carry foreign-tenant identity strings that the npm firewall gate never had to
# care about, because they are not in the npm `files` list and so were never on
# the npm publish surface. A bundle built without this file is a firewall breach.
#
# Keep this list in sync with the shipped set asserted by
# test/registry-manifests.mjs, which fails if any of these entries is dropped.

# Local session + agent scratch. Never ships anywhere.
.claude/
.tenant

# Build-time and test-time only. Not needed to RUN the server, and these are the
# files that carry foreign identity strings.
test/
scripts/

# Registry descriptors are read from the GitHub repo by the directories that
# want them; they do nothing inside a bundle.
server.json
smithery.yaml
glama.json

# Lockfile is for building this repo, not for running the bundled server.
package-lock.json

# Never, under any circumstances.
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store

# Bundles must not nest inside bundles.
*.mcpb
